      "emotion_agreement": true,
      "title": "Beware of packaging",
      "text": "I purchased a $50 gift card and had it sent to a relative. All of the online documentation indicated the recipient would not know what was in the package.  There was a box during the order process for a To: and From: and I also added \"Do Not Open Until Christmas\". The package arrived on the specified day but the label on the outside of the box did not have any indication of my note.  The recipient opened the box to find a sealed Amazon envelope and a packing slip.  The sealed envelope contained the gift card.  I figured the note should be here; nope.  I finally found the note on the packing slip.  OK, that's fine, but the packing slip also had the description of what was inside the sealed envelope including the denomination of the gift card; so much for a surprise."
